{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/234893-4th-edition","id":234893,"title":"4th Edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-19T18:46:04-07:00","id":234893,"title":"4th Edition?","content":"I mentioned this elsewhere, but I figured this would probably be a good place to isolate it as well...<br /> <br /> At the Gen Con &quot;Classic World of Darkness Q&amp;A&quot;, Rich happened to tease out two very eyebrow-raising words... &quot;<b>Fourth Edition</b>&quot;.<br /> It will be on the Eddy Webb audio-upload, and/or on the Darker Days video of the panel, but it was brought up (if I remember correctly) in the context of releasing some books as &quot;updates&quot; so as not having to necessarily wait until their 20th Anniversary editions.<br /> <br /> Now, chances are good that this was mostly just something to grab people's attentions, or throw out a far-fetched idea that everyone's been mulling over for nearly a decade now anyways (as well as to answer the already-answered question of &quot;is X20 actually 4th edition?&quot;)<br /> Releasing a 4th Edition seems a monumental task, and unless there is some amazing change to the system (like a central core rule book a la NWoD), it seems unlikely that they would still be producing X20 supplements while preparing to release a new edition of the same books.<br /> <br /> Still, it does bring up curious questions regarding how the plot would be handled (Mage: the Ascension Convention Books give a very nice blueprint for that), what sort of mechanics changes there might be, and if it would be best released as a &quot;patch&quot; than as a whole edition itself... Or should X20 just be officially revealed as &quot;The Fourth Edition&quot; officially?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T21:38:47-07:00","id":235040,"title":"","content":"I think the best choice would be to call the 20th books officially 4th edition. Next best would be to offer a cWoD core book 4e, which would be the equivalent of the &quot;patch&quot;, and could add the human element and a Base set of Abilities, attacks, defenses, equipment, and maybe a unifying feature like God-Machine or something. (I'm a big fan of the GM idea)<br /> <br /> Worst idea would be to actually release a new set of 4e books. I'm not buying the whole series again after 20th.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3651-grimmshade","name":"Grimmshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T22:55:17-07:00","id":235068,"title":"","content":"Yeah... a cWOD 4e that isn't just the 20th books seems way to early. We've still got C20, Wr20, and who knows if any of the post original cWOD books are getting similar treatment.<br /> <br /> I'd love an approach closer to the DA Revised line... but not immediately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T00:00:53-07:00","id":235121,"title":"","content":"Hm. In the context of releasing some books as updates? Thinking about it, it'd be most relevant for Reckoning and Fallen - H20 would be at least five years from now, while D20 would be at least eight years. If you wanted to release updated versions earlier, they wouldn't be part of the 20s, but nor would they be part of 1st, 2nd or Revised... which leaves 4th.<br /> <br /> (Mummy's in an interesting position, depending on which way you wanted to go with it; if you wanted to do Resurrection 20, that would be at least 7 years.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T03:28:07-07:00","id":235255,"title":"","content":"An update on par with GMC Chronicle would do good for the old line, since the mechanics, let's face it, need more than cosmetic tweaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T07:29:32-07:00","id":235391,"title":"","content":"If this would get me more Hunter the Reckoning material earlier than 2019, I'm all for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T07:45:08-07:00","id":235417,"title":"","content":"I'm not too fond of Reckoning's explanation for why Hunters pop up, but if the setting gives me options to make up what I would want, I'm okay with the re-release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T10:47:01-07:00","id":235574,"title":"","content":"The thing I see, regarding a possible Fourth Edition, is that each successive Twentieth Anniversary book has come closer to being a new edition than the previous one did. That is, the <b>V20</b> didn't have a LOT of revisions in it that would count it as a proper next edition. Yes, some Disciplines found tweaks, and there's changes to Clans and some Sects, but it has far fewer alterations than we saw from the first <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b> and the Second Edition, which was not a huge, sweeping change at that time. <b>Werewolf 20</b> changed enough from Revised Edition to really cheese-off folks on these boards (a clear sign of a proper new edition, if history is any indicator), and I see <b>M20</b> given a tremendous level of work on all fronts.<br /> <br /> When announced, <b>V20</b> was to be closer to a compendium of rules rather than a serious, company-wide return to the (classic) World of Darkness. The success of it allowed for some revisions to the game, and then it led to all of the resurrection of those lines \u2013 or that's how I remember it; do feel free to contradict me if I'm wrong. Please don't think that I have anything but love for <b>V20</b>, but also know that I can point out many instances of cut-and-paste copies from older books in that volume. Something like <i>The Hunters Hunted II</i> or <i>Rites of the Blood</i> IS a solid, completely revised book, no doubt. However, comparing <b>V20</b> to <b>M20</b> as being a 'fourth edition' is not a balanced equation, I think, at least not when looking at only those CORE books.<br /> <br /> ...Just my 2p on the issue. It's still an exciting prospect!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T20:25:38-07:00","id":237658,"title":"","content":"Rich and others have stated that V20 wasn't meant to be a full new version. If they had, they would have made more massive changes to the mechanics and setting. Instead, they went for trying to recreate what made V20 (and the later X20 books) so &quot;classic&quot; and combine the various versions into one. They made tough decisions not to change things too much just for that reason--it was a &quot;love letter&quot; to the fans who enjoyed the game over the last 20 years. (That's pretty much paraphrased from various posts over the years.)<br /> <br /> The 20th Anniversary Editions are a fourth edition (for most games, at least), but not the &quot;Fourth Edition&quot;. If it were to be a full &quot;Fourth Edition&quot;, we'd likely see a direct continuity of the setting (like we saw from the Convention Books from Mage: the Ascension Revised last year), and changes to mechanics that could be pretty significant. <br /> <br /> However, I think that we'd have to wait until C20 gets a year's worth of supplements under its belt before we ever saw anything officially announced as a &quot;Fourth Edition* to the Classic World of Darkness&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>*I assume that they'd just call another edition of Wraith and such &quot;Fourth Edition&quot; for the ease of it all.</i><br /> <br /> But, again, while it would be interesting to see what would happen if all of the Fat Splats existed in the very same realm, and a lot of players play it that way, it's not actually how the CWoD is created to be (much to a lot of our displeasure.) However, if they DID all exist in one... I wonder how that would actually affect the worlds of the games that we enjoy if mechanics were changed, and organizations re-organized so that they all existed together... how does the Technocracy and the Weaver and Will-Workers fit into the same metaphysical world. How does the Virtual Web, GW.net, and Schrecknet not all run into one another? How does God fit into the whole &quot;Weaver/Wyrm/Wyld/Gaia&quot; thing? How do you fit the timelines together with such huge discrepancies (without it being a pretty weak excuse like Demon tried... which worked... sorta... or at least was an attempt.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T21:10:58-07:00","id":237743,"title":"","content":"Man, it's kind of an exciting prospect. I'd love to see a Classic World of Darkness Core book that did all that. Took the best of each Core mechanic (Individual Weapon difficulties from Werewolf, Parry from Vampire, Armor from Mage, etc.) and then wove it all into a Core that would still work with all the 20th anniversary games. They could have a blended cosmology description, or better yet hints at how they may interact, and let the ST decide which were true, etc.<br /> That book could be used to create Humans, and have a lot of weapons and vehicles, etc.<br /> <br /> Probably won't happen, but it would be cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3651-grimmshade","name":"Grimmshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T00:25:18-07:00","id":237992,"title":"","content":"CWoD 4th Edition: &quot;Human: the nobodylikesyounobodywantsyouyou'reju